<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<SettingsFile xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/VisualStudio/2004/01/settings" CurrentProfile="(Default)" GeneratedClassNamespace="CFCLicensing.Properties" GeneratedClassName="Settings">
  <Profiles />
  <Settings>
    <Setting Name="EvaluationPeriod" Type="System.String" Scope="Application">
      <Value Profile="(Default)">I understand that I may use this software only for evaluation, and that any other use requires the purchase of a license.  You may license a registered copy of this software by contacting CFC Tech Services, Inc.  Click on the Order Information button below for contact information.</Value>
    </Setting>
    <Setting Name="SoftwareWarning" Type="System.String" Scope="Application">
      <Value Profile="(Default)">Warning: This computer software is protected by copyright law and 
international treaties.  Unauthorized reproduction or distribution of this 
software, or any portion of it, may result in severe civil and criminal penalties, 
and will be prosecuted to the maximum extent possible under the law.</Value>
    </Setting>
    <Setting Name="LicensedInformation" Type="System.String" Scope="Application">
      <Value Profile="(Default)">or call us at: 507-720-6600 

http://www.CFCTech.com</Value>
    </Setting>
    <Setting Name="LicensedVersion" Type="System.String" Scope="Application">
      <Value Profile="(Default)">To order a Licensed Version of this software, 
or extend the evaluation period for this Trial Version, 
send an email to CFC Tech Services, Inc. at: 

sales@CFCTech.com</Value>
    </Setting>
    <Setting Name="Instructions" Type="System.String" Scope="Application">
      <Value Profile="(Default)">Contact CFC Tech Services, Inc. for an Authorization Code 
for either Converting to a Licensed Version, or extending the 
Evaluation Period.   Make note of the Installation Code shown 
above.  You will be asked to provide this code in order to obtain 
a valid Authorization Code for Conversion or Extension.</Value>
    </Setting>
    <Setting Name="LicensedAgreement" Type="System.String" Scope="Application">
      <Value Profile="(Default)">NOTICE TO END USER:  This electronic end user agreement is a contract between you (either as an individual person or single legal entity) and CFC Tech Services, Inc. ('CFC').  Please read this agreement carefully.

By activating the license code and converting the software from a trial to an authorized license, you, ('Licensee') are consenting to be bound by all the terms and conditions of this Software License Agreement.

Licensee agrees that all system programs and documentation shall remain the confidential and proprietary property of CFC.  Licensee is entitled to the use of the software and documentation but acquires no rights to title or ownership of the property.

CFC software programs and their supporting documentation are protected by International Copyright laws.  Licensee will protect the proprietary and valuable property rights of CFC.

CFC will protect the proprietary rights of Licensee and will regard as secret and confidential any data and information furnished and designated as confidential by Licensee.

Licensee agrees that CFC property will not be altered, modified or adapted, including but not limited to translating, decompiling, disassembling or creating derivative works by anyone other than authorized CFC personnel. 

Licensee will not reproduce, distribute, rent, sub-license, lease, sublease, or otherwise transfer for value or cause to be transferred, CFC software programs and documentation without prior written consent of CFC.

Licensee agrees that 'Transfer of CFC software programs and documentation' includes use by an individual, separate entity, successor or assignee following an acquisition, merger, joint venture, affiliation or other consolidation between Licensee and another company or separate entity.

CFC agrees to provide customer services and software support to Licensee for a period of three (3) months at no charge.  These services include unlimited technical support by telephone, fax or e-mail from CFC offices in Minnesota between the hours of 8:00 a.m. (CT) and 5:00 p.m. (CT).  Licensee understands and agrees that charges may be incurred for service requests after 90 days.

CFC agrees to maintain the programs to include correcting any errors or malfunctions in the programs, free of charge for 90 days.  CFC shall not be liable for incidental or consequential damages resulting from the performance or use of this software.

Licensee understands and agrees that on-site training and/or consultation services are optional and must be contracted with CFC.</Value>
    </Setting>
    <Setting Name="SoftwareCompanyName" Type="System.String" Scope="Application">
      <Value Profile="(Default)">CFC Tech Demo</Value>
    </Setting>
